yes it's the home opener  yes they're about to get those world  series rings  but i think the thing that is most  special about today for a lot of us  is that this wonderful place  is about to get its voice back  so today  happily  i have the great pleasure  to introduce  the first  dodger manager  since my father  to receive the world series championship  ring  mr dave roberts  now it's time to bring out the members  of the 2020 world champion dodgers  here's cody bellinger you can finally  show him how much you love him  mookie betts one of the all-time greats  and now a world champion  clayton  kershaw the first ring for justin turner  [Applause]  congratulations one more time to the  2020 world champions the los angeles  dodgers  is one of the earliest meetings by  calendar date major league history that  the winners of each of the last two  world series have got together here in  the first weekend of the season with 26  year old 2019 all-star right-hander  walker bueller yeah it's a  growing list of how much better year to  year this guy gets i mean the resume  builder that he has already has  is going to be fun to watch as he  continues to climb the ladder and a lot  of records but  he's a fastball get after it bulldog  tight pitcher and he will  elevate the fastball  especially today  seven and a half strikeouts courtesy of  fed mgm we'll keep our eyes on that foul  pop  max muncie with that high sky there to  make the catch and there was the high  fastball in the upper part of the zone  that really has given broglie some  trouble trey turner off to a good start  homering in back-to-back games to start  the season  there's the next 3-2 pitch and another  fast ball shot to the right side of the  infield  3-3-2 pitches all of them fastballs  right on brand for walker bueller  he rarely swings early and he will take  his pitches because he's a master of the  strike zone  here is juan soto  got him on the high gas  a one two three start to the afternoon  for walker bueller showing off the  lively fastball joe ross on the mound  for the visiting nationals and john the  last time we saw him as we talked about  a moment ago  it was game five of the 2019 world  series yeah you take all that time off  and you  take on the defending champs welcome to  your first start  good slider to strike out chris taylor  here's corey seeger  caught looking this time  however two strikeouts start the  afternoon for joe ross  that's how you do it after a year and a  half  joe ross meanwhile unconcerned with fan  capacities or who uses what concession  stand of course he is off to a very good  start today  limiting the big swinging dodgers to  just a single their first time through  the order think about the last time we  saw him out there we kind of glanced  over this look it was game five of the  world series but he was not supposed to  start that night that's when max  scherzer woke up and couldn't move his  neck  and ross went out there and pitched  admirably over five innings as he is  this afternoon  he played three shutout innings in los  angeles so far a scoreless ball game top  of the fourth and trey turner leads  things off for the nationals turner soto  and zimmerman here for the gnats against  walker bueller  turner grounded out in his first try and  sends a fly ball into right here for  mckinstry running out of room may he  hangs on to make this catch  he is having a heck of a time with that  short wall in right and it angles right  obviously the more you go up and you're  just not prepared if it's taller you can  you can cushion the ball with your body  we talked about leading the league in  ops last year for soto at the age of 21  his career obs  972  over his three seasons  that one's past lux into right  that was a great example of being spread  out with two strikes  and doing what that young man does  better than any young player i've ever  seen come in the game including mike  trout the trouble with a guy like soto  is can you throw a third perfect pitch  he just makes you he does they they  don't he doesn't give you an easy strike  full count from walker bueller here's  the payoff pitch home  and there's a strike that's lined into  center field a two out single  well we called the last two out two on  opportunity for the nationals their best  opportunity to score but it set up the  number nine spot of the order this is an  even better opportunity now with starlin  castro  02.  and a curveball that's bounced to the  left side turner's got it  you know what he ended with 90 pitches  again i'm amazed at the outing that joe  ross had  what a great job for him  five scoreless innings struck out four  allowed two singles to walk two batters  in his first start since october of  2019. justin turner now he is  responsible for both of the dodgers hits  in this game two singles against joe  ross justin turner lifts off a high  drive out to left center field and that  one's gone  justin turner is a one-man band this  afternoon in l.a  all three dodger hits and the only run  of the day  courtesy of their 12-year veteran third  baseman that's amazing 0 for 16 the rest  of the lineup justin turner who got  resigned got his ring  walker bueller gone after 90 pitches and  six shutout innings in favor of  left-hander victor gonzalez so bueller  clean over six innings six singles got  out of a couple of two out jams no walks  in a very good afternoon will be a first  time meeting between former teammates  trinin and ryan zimmerman  zimmerman shoots it back up the middle  dodgers hadn't played perfectly and  despite having runners at the corners  and nobody out the nationals are turned  away in the eighth  former milwaukee teammates to  potentially decide an outcome here in  los angeles this afternoon  and the defending world series champs  improved to six and two with a  one-nothing shutout win in their 2021  home opener

